{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-1991",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-1991: Important priority package update for rpm",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-07-20 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-07-20 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-44605:\n\tA heap buffer overflow exists in RPM's NDB database backend (lib/backend/ndb/rpmpkg.c) due to unchecked 32-bit arithmetic when parsing the slot table. The slotnpages value is read directly from the on-disk NDB header and used in a 32-bit multiplication (slotnpages * (PAGE_SIZE / SLOT_SIZE)) to size a heap allocation. A crafted Packages.db can supply a slotnpages value that wraps this product to a small number, causing xcalloc to allocate an undersized buffer. The subsequent loop iterates over the full unwrapped page count, writing pkgslot entries past the heap boundary before per-slot validation runs. Exploitation requires the victim to open a crafted NDB database file with RPM tooling, and NDB is not the default backend in Fedora or RHEL (both default to sqlite).\n",
